\begin_inset LatexCommand \label{sub:hexedit}

\end_inset 

The Hex editor
\layout Standard

The Hex editor is pretty much the same in all games, though the keys to
 access the 128k memory banks only apply in 128k games.
 
\layout Standard


\emph on 
Be warned that it's very easy to damage your game beyond repair using the
 Hex editor.
 Only use it if you are sure you know what you are doing!
\layout Standard

When using the Hex editor, remember the following:
\layout Enumerate

Any outstanding changes you make are shown in magenta.
 Until you click 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset 

Write
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset 

 (or press Control-W), they will not be applied to the game.
\layout Enumerate

You can click 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset 

Undo
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset 

 (or press Control-Z) to remove all outstanding changes.
\layout Enumerate

Switching to another screen and back also removes all outstanding changes.
\layout Standard

The Hex editor displays three columns of data.
 The left column gives addresses; the middle column gives the hex values
 of the bytes at those addresses; and the right column gives ASCII equivalents
 (if any).
 Values that can't be edited (such as bytes which would not be saved in
 a snapshot) are shown in blue.
 The bottom bar shows the address that the cursor is currently on.
\layout Standard

The following keys can be used:
\layout Description

Cursors: Move left/right/up/down.
\layout Description

Page\SpecialChar ~
Up\SpecialChar ~
/\SpecialChar ~
Page\SpecialChar ~
Down: Move up/down a page (27 lines) at a time.
\layout Description

Home\SpecialChar ~
/\SpecialChar ~
End: Move to the start/end of the current line.
\layout Description

Shift+Home\SpecialChar ~
/\SpecialChar ~
Shift+End: Move to addresses 0 and 0FFFFh respectively.
\layout Description

Tab: Switches between the 'hex' and 'text' columns.
 
\layout Description

Control-A: Enter address.
 This moves the cursor to the specified address.
\layout Description

Control-F: Find bytes.
 Enter a sequence of Hex bytes to find.
 The search will start at the byte after the current one.
\layout Description

Control-G: Find again.
 Repeats the last search, starting at the byte after the current one.
 You can also use F3 to get the same effect.
\layout Description

Control-W: Write data.
 All outstanding changes (shown in magenta) are applied to the game.
\layout Description

Control-Z: Undo.
 All outstanding changes are reversed.
\layout Description

Control-0\SpecialChar ~
to\SpecialChar ~
Control-7: Select memory bank at 0C000h.
 For 128k games only.
 Note that banks 5 and 2 are always present at 4000h and 8000h respectively.
\layout Description

Other\SpecialChar ~
keys: If the cursor is in the 'hex' column, 0-9 and A-F allow the Hex
 values to be modified.
 If it's in the 'text' column, then any key producing an ASCII value will
 insert that value at the current location.
 This includes ALT+P for Copyright.
\layout Section


\begin_inset LatexCommand \label{sec: gedit}

\end_inset 

The Guardian editor
\layout Subsection

On Guardian Classes
\layout Standard

In Jet Set Willy games (other than JSW64), guardians in a room are drawn
 from a table of guardian classes, with up to 127 entries (Softricks games
 have 255 entries in their guardian table; 128k games can have more than
 one guardian table).
 
\layout Standard

The guardian editor operates on the entries in this table.
 So if you change a guardian that's present in more than one room, you'll
 find that it changes in all the rooms that have the guardian.
 For example, in the original JSW, changing the flag in 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset 

On top of the house
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset 

 will also affect the moon-faced guardian in 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset 

Under the Drive
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset 

.
\layout Subsection

Editor overview
\layout Standard

When a guardian is being edited, the top half of the screen shows a preview
 of the result, while the bottom half contains controls.
 The controls shown vary for different guardian types, but include:
